Object.assign(window.IND_FEED_BODY, {"en-ramayana-13-7":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|13","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":13},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:12:cards:7:text","title":"The Ramayana · The Berries Shabari Kept","body":"\"They are not all sweet,\" said Shabari, not looking up, working through the pile. \"You cannot tell from the outside. I am not giving him a sour one. He has walked a long way.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 13","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","13 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-13-8":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|13","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":13},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:12:cards:8:text","title":"The Ramayana · The Berries Shabari Kept","body":"Rama took the plate out of her hands and ate every berry on it, one after another, and then reached over and took the ones she had not tested yet as well. \"These are the best thing I have eaten in fourteen years,\" he said, and he was not being kind. He meant it.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 13","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","13 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-13-9":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|13","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":13},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:12:cards:9:text","title":"The Ramayana · The Berries Shabari Kept","body":"She asked about Sita. They told her. She thought for a while and then said, \"Go to Pampa lake, down there where the blue is. There are monkeys on that hill who have lost a kingdom themselves. People who have lost something are the ones who help.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 13","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","13 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-13-10":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|13","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":13},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:12:cards:10:text","title":"The Ramayana · The Berries Shabari Kept","body":"They stayed that night. In the morning she had gone — in some tellings into a fire she made herself, in others simply gone, the way people in this story go when they have finished. The flowers were on the path. She had swept it before she left.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 13","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","13 of 24"]]},"en-mahabharata-6-1":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|6","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":6},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:5:cards:1:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Cousins Who Could Not Be Friends","body":"He would climb a tree with all of them in it and shake the branch until they fell out like fruit. He would hold four of them underwater in the river and count. He always let go. They always came up. And every single time, a hundred boys walked home dripping and humiliated in front of the whole city.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 6","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","6 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-6-2":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|6","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":6},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:5:cards:2:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Cousins Who Could Not Be Friends","body":"Duryodhana went to his uncle Shakuni, his mother's brother, who had come to Hastinapura for the wedding and somehow never gone home. Shakuni listened to everything. Shakuni was extremely good at listening.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 6","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","6 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-6-3":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|6","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":6},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:5:cards:3:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Cousins Who Could Not Be Friends","body":"\"Say it out loud,\" said Shakuni. \"All of it. Nobody will hear you but me.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 6","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","6 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-6-4":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|6","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":6},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:5:cards:4:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Cousins Who Could Not Be Friends","body":"\"My father is the elder brother,\" said Duryodhana. \"My father was passed over because of his eyes, which he did not choose. I was born in this house. That throne came to me down the older line and everybody in this court knows it.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 6","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","6 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-6-6":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|6","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":6},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:5:cards:6:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Cousins Who Could Not Be Friends","body":"Here is the thing the poem does that most stories will not do for you. It does not tell him he is wrong. He is not entirely wrong. He has a real complaint, and he has had it since he was small, and not one grown-up in that palace ever sat down and dealt with it honestly.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 6","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","6 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-6-7":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|6","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":6},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:5:cards:7:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Cousins Who Could Not Be Friends","body":"What they did instead was tell him to stop making a fuss, and go on adoring the cousins, in front of him, for years.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 6","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","6 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-6-8":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|6","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":6},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:5:cards:8:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Cousins Who Could Not Be Friends","body":"And then one summer there was a picnic by the river. Bhima ate enough for six people, as usual, and went to sleep on the bank, as usual. And when he woke up he was in deep water in the dark, a long way down.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 6","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","6 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-6-9":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|6","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":6},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:5:cards:9:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Cousins Who Could Not Be Friends","body":"He came home three days later, covered in weed, twice as strong as he had gone out and in a filthy mood. Nobody was punished. Nobody was even asked. The palace decided, the way palaces do, that it was better not to have found out.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 6","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","6 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-7-1":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|7","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":7},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:6:cards:1:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Ring in the Well","body":"A thin man in poor clothes had been watching from the shade. \"Princes,\" he said. \"Sons of the greatest house in the world. Defeated by a hole.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 7","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","7 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-7-2":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|7","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":7},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:6:cards:2:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Ring in the Well","body":"He picked a blade of grass, said something over it, and dropped it. It went down and stuck in the ball. Then he dropped a second blade, which stuck in the first. Then a third. He built a chain of grass down that well and pulled the ball out with it while the princes watched with their mouths open.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 7","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","7 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-7-3":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|7","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":7},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:6:cards:3:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Ring in the Well","body":"Then he took a ring off his own finger, threw it down the well, and got that out too, just to make the point twice. \"Go and tell Bhishma what you saw,\" he said, and sat back down in the shade.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 7","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","7 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-7-4":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|7","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":7},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:6:cards:4:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Ring in the Well","body":"Bhishma came at a run, because he already knew who it had to be. His name was Drona, and he was probably the finest teacher of weapons alive, and he was standing outside the palace in torn clothes because he had nothing.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 7","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","7 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-7-5":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|7","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":7},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:6:cards:5:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Ring in the Well","body":"Here is the piece of Drona you need. When he was young his closest friend was a boy called Drupada, who used to say they would share everything when he was king. Years later Drona, hungry, went to remind him. Drupada laughed at him in front of his whole court, and said that kings are not friends with poor men, and had him shown out.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 7","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","7 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-7-7":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|7","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":7},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:6:cards:7:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Ring in the Well","body":"He took the school. And of all of them, the one who could do what he could do was Arjuna, who practised in the dark just to find out whether he could, and who followed him about like a dog.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 7","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","7 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-7-8":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|7","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":7},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:6:cards:8:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Ring in the Well","body":"One day Drona hung a wooden bird in a tree and called them up one at a time. \"Aim at the eye,\" he said. \"Now tell me what you see.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 7","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","7 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-7-9":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|7","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":7},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:6:cards:9:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Ring in the Well","body":"\"I see the tree, the branch, the bird, you, my brothers—\" \"Step back,\" said Drona. He said it eleven times. Then Arjuna came up and drew.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 7","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","7 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-7-10":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|7","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":7},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:6:cards:10:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Ring in the Well","body":"\"What do you see?\" \"The eye.\" \"And the bird?\" \"No. The eye.\" \"And the tree, and me, and your brothers?\" \"There is only the eye,\" said Arjuna, and Drona said, very quietly, \"Shoot,\" and that was the end of the lesson.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 7","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","7 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-8-1":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|8","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":8},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:7:cards:1:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Ekalavya","body":"He put his head on the ground in front of Drona. \"Teach me the bow,\" he said. \"I will do anything. I will sweep. I will carry. I have wanted this since I was small.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 8","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","8 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-8-2":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|8","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":8},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:7:cards:2:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Ekalavya","body":"\"No,\" said Drona. He said it mildly, the way you decline a second helping. \"This is the school of the princes of Hastinapura. You are a forest chief's son. Go home.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 8","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","8 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-8-3":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|8","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":8},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:7:cards:3:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Ekalavya","body":"That is the sentence. Read it again if you like. It is not shouted and it is not explained and nobody in the courtyard objects to it, and the boy who has walked for days stands up and walks back out through the gate.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 8","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","8 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-8-4":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|8","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":8},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:7:cards:4:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Ekalavya","body":"He did not go home in a rage. He went into the forest and he made a figure of Drona out of clay and river mud, roughly, the way you would, having seen a man once. He put it under a tree. He put flowers on it in the morning.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 8","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","8 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-8-5":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|8","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":8},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:7:cards:5:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Ekalavya","body":"And then he taught himself, in front of it, for years. Alone. No teacher, no corrections, nobody to tell him he was improving. Just a clay man under a tree and a boy who would not stop.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 8","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","8 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-8-6":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|8","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":8},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:7:cards:6:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Ekalavya","body":"Years later a royal hunting party came through that part of the forest, and one of the dogs ran ahead and started barking, on and on, at something in the trees.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 8","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","8 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-8-8":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|8","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":8},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:7:cards:8:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Ekalavya","body":"Arjuna went white. He had spent his whole life being told he was the finest archer in the world, and he had just been shown something he could not do. Drona took one look at the dog and went into the trees to find whoever had done it.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 8","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","8 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-8-9":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|8","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":8},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:7:cards:9:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Ekalavya","body":"The boy was on his feet before they reached him, and down on the ground at Drona's feet before anybody could speak. \"You came,\" he said. \"Teacher.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 8","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","8 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-8-10":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|8","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":8},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:7:cards:10:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Ekalavya","body":"\"Who taught you?\" said Drona. Ekalavya pointed at the clay figure under the tree, with the flowers on it, and said, \"You did.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 8","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","8 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-8-11":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|8","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":8},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:7:cards:11:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Ekalavya","body":"And Drona looked at him and said, \"Then I will have my teacher's fee. I will have the thumb of your right hand.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 8","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","8 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-8-12":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|8","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":8},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:7:cards:12:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Ekalavya","body":"The boy did not argue and did not hesitate and did not ask why. He cut off his right thumb and put it in his teacher's hands, and then he bowed, and Arjuna was the finest archer in the world again by the time they rode home.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 8","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","8 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-9-1":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|9","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":9},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:8:cards:1:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Young Man at the Gate","body":"Then Arjuna came out and the arena stopped arguing. He put out fire with water arrows and made water with fire ones. He shot twenty-one arrows into a moving cow-horn. People stood on their seats.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 9","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","9 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-9-2":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|9","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":9},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:8:cards:2:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Young Man at the Gate","body":"And into all that noise, through the gate, walked a young man nobody knew, in golden armour that seemed to be part of him, with earrings to match.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 9","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","9 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-9-3":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|9","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":9},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:8:cards:3:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Young Man at the Gate","body":"\"He did not stop at the gate,\" a guard said afterwards, still baffled. \"They all stop at the gate. He walked straight past me like he had been coming here his whole life.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 9","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","9 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-9-4":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|9","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":9},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:8:cards:4:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Young Man at the Gate","body":"He went to the middle and did everything Arjuna had just done. Not roughly. Exactly. The arena went completely silent, which is a much bigger compliment than cheering.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 9","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","9 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-9-5":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|9","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":9},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:8:cards:5:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Young Man at the Gate","body":"\"Anything he can do, I can do,\" he said to Drona. \"Give me him.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 9","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","9 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-9-6":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|9","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":9},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:8:cards:6:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Young Man at the Gate","body":"Duryodhana was on his feet with both arms in the air. Arjuna's face had gone still. And then one of the old teachers stepped forward and asked the polite, ordinary, procedural question that you have to ask before two men fight in front of a king.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 9","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","9 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-9-8":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|9","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":9},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:8:cards:8:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Young Man at the Gate","body":"The young man opened his mouth and nothing came out. In the gallery, Kunti had gone the colour of the cloth she was holding, and had put her hand on the rail, and had said nothing at all.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 9","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","9 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-9-9":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|9","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":9},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:8:cards:9:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Young Man at the Gate","body":"And then Duryodhana walked down into the arena, in front of everybody, and said: \"Then I will fix it. I do not care whose son he is. I have watched him shoot. The kingdom of Anga is mine to give and I am giving it to him. Now. Somebody fetch water and a crown.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 9","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","9 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-9-10":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|9","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":9},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:8:cards:10:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Young Man at the Gate","body":"They crowned him on the spot, in the dust, while the arena watched. And into the middle of it walked an old charioteer, shaking, who had heard the noise and come to find his boy — and Karna went straight over and put his head on the old man's feet in front of thirty thousand people.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 9","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","9 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-9-11":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|9","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":9},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:8:cards:11:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Young Man at the Gate","body":"Somebody laughed. Bhima said something about the chariot-drivers' lane that he would still be paying for eighteen years later. And Karna, who had a kingdom now and had never had anything, turned and looked at Duryodhana with an expression he kept for the rest of his life.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 9","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","9 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-9-12":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|9","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":9},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:8:cards:12:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Young Man at the Gate","body":"Then the sun went down, and by the rules the fight could not be held, and everybody went home. It was the kindest thing anybody does in this entire poem. It was also the thing that bought the war.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 9","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","9 of 33"]]}});
